# What Prettier must NOT touch, and why. Every line here is a decision, not a
# default: an ignore file that grows by habit is how a style gate stops meaning
# anything.

# Build output. `npm run build` writes it, `tools/emit-route-cards.mjs` rewrites
# the emitted HTML afterwards, and nothing in it is reviewed by a human. Without
# this line `npm run check:format` passes on a clean checkout and fails right
# after a build, which would teach everyone to ignore the gate.
dist/

# npm owns the lockfile. It is machine-written on every install, and reformatting
# it would put the gate in a fight it cannot win.
package-lock.json

# Two reasons, and the second one is the one that matters. First: the bridge
# Claude writes through rejects `.github/`, so a block cannot fix a finding here.
# Second, measured on 13-oct: the ONLY thing Prettier changes in this whole
# directory is one continuation line of an HTML comment in
# `pull_request_template.md`, which it indents eight spaces deeper -- a change
# that makes the file harder to read, not easier. So this is not a gap waiting
# to be closed by hand: it is a decision. Revisit it if Prettier's markdown
# output ever earns it.
.github/
